findings.suggestion:
Extract a `buildAbilities(input: BuildAbilitiesInput): Abilities<AlertRuleAction>` pure function that takes the resolved primitives and returns the abilities object. Each hook gathers its own primitives (editability, silence, permissions, rule-type flags) and calls `buildAbilities`. This reduces duplication, centralizes the action→ability mapping, and makes the two hooks' behavioral differences explicit in their input parameters. Example:
```ts
function buildAbilities(input: {
  isEditable?: boolean; isRemovable?: boolean;
  isProvisioned: boolean; isFederated: boolean; isPluginProvided: boolean;
  isAlertingRule: boolean; maybeSupported: boolean; exportAllowed: boolean;
  rulesPermissions: RulesPermissions; silence: Ability;
}): Abilities<AlertRuleAction> { /* single implementation */ }
```
